    "updated_at": "2026-11-19T16:55:16Z",
    "body": "STOPPED: the required validation failed twice. Claim released.\n\nThe new machine_model module generates closed travel boxes and spindle cylinders. It composes linear and rotary joints, marks generated bodies, notes missing figures, and refuses invalid input by name. The held patch is uncommitted in /home/mikekinney/CamcraftCodex/.claude/worktrees/issue-2584 on issue/2584-machine-model, based on upstream/main e5b0ca3c1. Nothing was pushed and no PR was opened.\n\nAll ten machine_model pins pass. The unchanged-code run failed because the module was absent. Replacing lib.rs with upstream's version failed, and restoration passed. Sixteen behavioral guard mutations each failed at runtime and passed after restoration. All mutations are restored. No G-code or golden files changed. PR #2763 touches lib.rs for a different module declaration.\n\ncargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main passed twice. cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings failed first on collapsible_if in build.rs; that is fixed. The second run failed on six err_expect warnings in crates/sim/tests/machine_model/refusals.rs at lines 68, 108, 145, 152, 172, and 215. Those test chains need expect_err() instead of err().expect(). I stopped under the two-failure rule before changing them. Step 8 and Step 9 were not reached.\n\nLocal evidence is outside the branch at /tmp/2584-before.log, /tmp/2584-mutation-summary.txt, /tmp/2584-gate.log, and /tmp/2584-clippy.log. The issue is free again.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
